## The Needle (Bug Found)

The deadlock is in `app/TransferService.java` lines 25-31. The code locks accounts in parameter order:
- `synchronized (from.getLock())` first
- `synchronized (to.getLock())` second

This causes deadlock when concurrent transfers happen in opposite directions:
- Thread 1: A→B (locks A, waits for B)
- Thread 2: B→A (locks B, waits for A)

## The Fix

Replace the locking strategy with consistent lock ordering based on account ID:

```java
// Determine lock order based on account ID to prevent deadlock
Account first, second;
if (from.getId().compareTo(to.getId()) < 0) {
    first = from;
    second = to;
} else {
    first = to;
    second = from;
}

// Lock accounts in consistent order
synchronized (first.getLock()) {
    try { Thread.sleep(1); } catch (InterruptedException e) {
        Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
    }

    synchronized (second.getLock()) {
        // Rest of transfer logic...
    }
}
```

This ensures all threads acquire locks in the same order (alphabetically by account ID), preventing circular wait conditions.

## Verification

The fix should allow `test.sh` to pass by:
1. Preventing deadlocks in concurrent bidirectional transfers
2. Maintaining balance conservation
3. Completing all transfers within the timeout

